
        Decorator Design Pattern (ELI10)

Imagine you have a plain pizza 🍕.

Plain pizza = Base object
Add cheese = Decorator
Add olives = Another decorator
Add mushrooms = Yet another decorator

You keep wrapping the pizza with extra toppings without changing the original pizza class.

That's exactly what the Decorator Pattern does:
    It adds new behavior to an object dynamically without modifying the object's code.


Example: Vehicle Features
    
1. Component Interface
    interface Vehicle {
        String getDescription();
    }

2. Concrete Component
    class BasicCar implements Vehicle {
        @Override
        public String getDescription() {
            return "Basic Car";
        }
    }

3. abstract Decorator
    abstract class VehicleDecorator implements Vehicle {
        protected Vehicle vehicle;
        public VehicleDecorator(Vehicle vehicle) {
            this.vehicle = vehicle;
        }
    }

4. Concrete Decorators
Electric Feature

    class ElectricDecorator extends VehicleDecorator {

        public ElectricDecorator(Vehicle vehicle) {
            super(vehicle);
        }

        @Override
        public String getDescription() {
            return vehicle.getDescription() + " + Electric System";
        }
    }

 Hybrid Feature
    class HybridDecorator extends VehicleDecorator {

        public HybridDecorator(Vehicle vehicle) {
            super(vehicle);
        }

        @Override
        public String getDescription() {
            return vehicle.getDescription() + " + Hybrid System";
        }
    }


5. Client

    public class Main {

        public static void main(String[] args) {

            Vehicle car = new BasicCar();
            System.out.println(car.getDescription());

            Vehicle electricCar =
                    new ElectricDecorator(new BasicCar());
            System.out.println(electricCar.getDescription());

            Vehicle hybridCar =
                    new HybridDecorator(new BasicCar());
            System.out.println(hybridCar.getDescription());
        }
    }


Output
Basic Car
Basic Car + Electric System
Basic Car + Hybrid System


UML class diagram:-
----------------------
              Vehicle
                 ^
                 |
        +----------------+
        |    BasicCar    |
        +----------------+

              Vehicle
                 ^
